title: Foreign Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; foreign_policy_timer += 8
view-if: spd_in_government = 1 and foreign_minister_party = "SPD" and  foreign_policy_timer <= 0
card-image: img/portraits/BreitscheidRudolf.jpg
go-to: fp_menu

= Foreign Policy

Russia's war against Ukraine is in its [? if year <= 2029 : fifth ?][? if year > 2029 : sixth or later ?] year, the United States is an unpredictable ally, and China is both our largest trading partner and a rival. What should our foreign policy priority be?

@fp_menu

- @improve_west
- @improve_east
- @improve_soviet
- @customs_union
- @expose
- @european_union
- @european_union_2
- @support_austria
- @root: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@improve_west
title: Revive the Franco-German partnership.
on-arrival: west_relation += 2

Paris and Berlin have often blocked each other in recent years, on energy, defence and trade. We agree on common positions before every European summit again, and the joint cabinet meetings return.

@improve_east
title: Improve our relations with Poland, the Baltic states and Ukraine.
on-arrival: east_relation += 2

Our eastern neighbours have not forgotten that Germany ignored their warnings about Russia for years. We listen more, visit more, and settle old disputes. Warsaw notices the change.

@improve_soviet
title: Decide our policy towards Russia and the war.

The SPD was the party of Ostpolitik, and for many of our older members, talking to Moscow is part of our identity. But after 2022, few believe that Putin can be trusted. What should we do?

- @soviet_economic_aid_yes_mil: Increase military aid for Ukraine.
- @soviet_economic_aid_yes: Push for ceasefire talks.
- @soviet_economic_aid_no: Keep our current course.

@soviet_economic_aid_yes_mil
choose-if: budget >= 1
subtitle: -1 budget
on-arrival: budget -= 1; russia_relation -= 1; east_relation += 2; west_relation += 1; left_dissent += 4; linke_relation -= 4; reformist_dissent -= 3; bundeswehr_loyalty += 0.02

We send more air defence and ammunition to Ukraine and fund its arms industry. Kyiv, Warsaw and the Baltic states are grateful. Part of our membership worries that we are being drawn into the war.

@soviet_economic_aid_yes
on-arrival: russia_relation += 1; east_relation -= 2; west_relation -= 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition; left_dissent -= 4; reformist_dissent += 5; linke_relation += 3; bsw_relation += 3; foreign_goal_completed += 1

Together with Brazil and the Vatican, we propose a framework for ceasefire talks. Moscow is noncommittal, and Kyiv is suspicious. Our eastern neighbours warn against a peace over Ukraine's head, while the peace wing of our party is pleased.

@soviet_economic_aid_no

We keep supporting Ukraine at the current level and keep the channels to Moscow open, without big announcements.

@customs_union
title: Negotiate with Washington over trade and tariffs.
on-arrival: us_relation += 1; economic_growth += 0.1 if us_relation >= 1; west_relation -= 1 if us_relation >= 2

German carmakers and machine builders depend on the American market, and Washington keeps threatening new tariffs. We send delegations, buy more American liquefied gas, and try to keep the European Commission on side. [? if us_relation >= 2 : Paris accuses us of making side deals. ?]

@expose
title: Pass a strict arms export control law.
view-if: rearmament_exposed == 0
on-arrival: rearmament_exposed += 1; pacifism += 1; linke_relation += 4*(1-dissent); greens_relation += 2*(1-dissent); left_dissent -= 4; reformist_dissent += 4; cdu_relation -= 3; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition; foreign_goal_completed += 1; economic_growth -= 0.1

No more arms for dictatorships and war zones, with exceptions only for allies and for countries defending themselves, such as Ukraine. The arms industry warns about lost orders, and the Union says it ties our hands.

@european_union
title: Push for a European investment and defence union.
subtitle: Common borrowing for defence and the energy transition, and majority voting in foreign policy.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if west_relation < 4 : Our relations with France and the West are not good enough. ?] [? if east_relation < 3 : Our relations with our eastern neighbours are not good enough. ?]
view-if: eu_progress < 2 and eu = 0
choose-if: west_relation >= 4 and east_relation >= 3
on-arrival: eu_progress += 1; west_relation += 1; fdp_relation -= 3

A federal Europe has been in the SPD's programme since 1925. We put a concrete proposal on the table: a permanent European fund for defence and the energy transition, paid for with common bonds, and an end to the veto in foreign policy. The frugal countries in the north are sceptical.

@european_union_2
title: We can sign a treaty to reform the European Union!
view-if: west_relation >= 4 and east_relation >= 3 and eu_progress >= 2 and eu = 0
on-arrival: eu = 1; unemployment_rate -= 0.3 if unemployment_rate >= 6; inflation -= 0.2 if inflation >= 3; workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 4*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent); rural_spd += 2*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 2*(1-dissent); trust_in_democracy += 3; nationalism -= 3; budget += 1; economic_growth += 0.3; afd_relation -= 5
max-visits: 1
achievement: eu

The heads of government sign the treaty in Strasbourg. Europe can now borrow together for its defence and its energy transition, and a single country can no longer block its foreign policy. The AfD calls it the end of German sovereignty. Most Germans see it differently.

@support_austria
title: Defend the rule of law in the European Union.
subtitle: Cut EU funds for governments that undermine the courts and the free press.
on-arrival: left_dissent -= 3; center_dissent -= 3; west_relation += 1; afd_relation -= 2
max-visits: 3

We push the Commission to freeze EU funds for governments that attack their courts and their free press, and we back civil society groups in those countries.
